00:00:36.698 --> 00:00:38.056
- Hi Leo.
- Hi Leo.

00:00:38.056 --> 00:00:40.006
- Hi Sarah, hi Sophia, hi Drew.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.763
How are you guys?

00:00:41.763 --> 00:00:42.596
- Good.

00:00:42.596 --> 00:00:45.242
- Leo, take over the segment.

00:00:45.242 --> 00:00:46.075
- If you say so.

00:00:46.075 --> 00:00:47.340
- I do say so.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.160
It's my dear, dear,
dear friend, Leo Kelly.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.760
I love you so much, Leo!
(audience applauds)

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.790
And Sarah, we've done
the show together before.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:00:59.623
- Yes, ma'm.

00:00:59.623 --> 00:01:00.500
- What are we making today?

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.320
- Well, we're gonna reuse some things

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.310
to make some cool stuff
for our room, right Leo?

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:05.143
- [Leo] I like re-using.

00:01:05.143 --> 00:01:06.160
- I like re-using too.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.390
Super important, okay.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.160
So one thing I've noticed, being a mom,

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.520
or maybe not being a mom,

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.500
is book jackets on your
kids' books, right?

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.800
They come off, they get ripped.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.310
But I like to keep the book jacket,

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:16.650
we don't wanna throw it away.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.640
So all you need for this is a container

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.473
from around your house,

00:01:19.473 --> 00:01:21.850
it could be like, protein
canister or something

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:22.683
from the kitchen.

00:01:22.683 --> 00:01:24.470
You take the lid, you
take all the labels off,

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:25.480
clean it up, and you take the lid,

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.640
cut a hole.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.280
Exacto knife, but be careful
with those kid fingers.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.980
And then, everyone in front of you guys

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.090
have a book jacket.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.940
You wanna open up your book jacket,

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:36.450
and take a little bit
of double sided tape,

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.210
and we're gonna start on our end

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.030
that has not your main picture on it.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.270
And we're gonna just put that little bit

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:45.770
of double sided tape on the inside piece.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:46.870
Then what you're gonna do is

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.010
you're gonna start with that piece

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:50.520
and we're gonna wrap it
around our container.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.030
And then you just grab
another little piece

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.950
of double sided tape, you
guys, it's super easy.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.140
And you just put that
right on your last piece.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:58.980
Just like that, you got it, Leo.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:01:59.813
Good job.

00:01:59.813 --> 00:02:00.780
Drew, you got it.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.610
And there you go, you got a little themed

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:04.443
piggy bank.
(audience applauds)

00:02:04.443 --> 00:02:06.338
Or you could put tissues in it, right?

00:02:06.338 --> 00:02:07.171
- [Leo] I like it.

00:02:07.171 --> 00:02:08.850
- Oh, it's a piggy bank!

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.098
- This is cute.

00:02:10.098 --> 00:02:11.330
- You got it, that's perfect.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.847
Okay, so up next, we're
gonna do some tassels.

00:02:12.847 --> 00:02:15.320
So I love a good tassel wall.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.570
I like to string them on a
string and hang them on a wall.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.740
I think it adds a really fun pop of color.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.320
- [Drew] I like, in front
of our table right here,

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.140
we have beautiful tassels hanging.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.970
- And these are made
out of t-shirts, y'all.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:27.820
All you have to do is thrift some tees,

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.910
or your old tees, you wanna cut strips.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.280
So this one that we're gonna be doing

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.810
is about seven feet long.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.020
And so you wanna take your long strip,

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.070
you kind of stretch it out.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.740
Take your book and take your long

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:41.310
stretched out, stringy piece of t-shirt.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.720
And we're gonna start with that,

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:43.950
the bottom of the string,

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:45.290
right at the bottom of the book.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.460
And then you're just gonna
wrap it around, guys.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.340
That's it.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.173
- [Sophia] Ooh.

00:02:49.173 --> 00:02:50.930
- Just wrap. You got it, Leo.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:51.763
There you go.

00:02:51.763 --> 00:02:53.820
That's all you do, you
come around and you wrap.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.392
Now remember, the bigger the
book, the longer the tassel,

00:02:56.392 --> 00:02:57.950
the more times you wrap it,

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.014
the thicker the tassel's gonna be.

00:03:00.014 --> 00:03:01.940
And you could customize these, right, Leo?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.140
Didn't you say your brother's into Batman?

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.160
You could make him a black and yellow one.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.490
So once you come around,

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:07.510
then what you're gonna do is you're gonna

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:08.540
take this little string.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.240
You've got one little extra string.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.630
You're gonna come up over the
top of the book like this.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:14.820
And you're just gonna tie that off.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.673
That's gonna hold all of your pieces.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.370
In place. You got it.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:20.954
Okay, so then once you
get it tied like that,

00:03:20.954 --> 00:03:22.367
check it out.
- Ah.

00:03:23.343 --> 00:03:24.311
- You got it?

00:03:24.311 --> 00:03:25.576
- I'm in the process.

00:03:25.576 --> 00:03:26.409
- [Sophia] Do you just tie it in a knot?

00:03:26.409 --> 00:03:27.260
- Yeah, just tie it in a knot.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.093
Just like that.

00:03:28.093 --> 00:03:29.950
